From bb4e99cd1838dcf64d4ba50fb12cd101036ed015 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mojavemesa-lgtm <252102886+mojavemesa-lgtm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:32:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm845-oneplus: Lower
 op-sink-microwatt to 5 W

The connector's op-sink-microwatt of 15 W is higher than what the 5 V
sink PDO can supply. When the phone requests the first (5 V) fixed PDO
of a source offering 5 V / 2.4 A, tcpm then sets the Capability Mismatch
bit in the request, since 15 W is more than 5 V * 2.4 A.

An Anker iQ3 PD charger (5 V 2.4 A / 9 V 3 A / 15 V 3 A / 20 V 2.25 A)
reacts to that by sending a Hard Reset about 450 ms after PS_RDY, then
comes back, accepts again, and resets again: a storm of about 20 s until
the contract finally sticks. This happens on every replug of the charger.

Set the operating sink power to 5 W, which is what the phone wants from
a 5 V contract. The request no longer carries the mismatch bit.

Tested on a OnePlus 6T (fajita) with the same Anker PD charger: with 15 W
the storm was reproduced after replugs; with 5 W there were 0 hard
resets and a clean 5 V / 2.4 A PD 3.0 contract. Only this one PD
charger model was tested, and few replugs.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-oneplus-common.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-oneplus-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-oneplus-common.dtsi
index e9a68e4dc..f4f1216bc 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-oneplus-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-oneplus-common.dtsi
@@ -966,7 +966,7 @@ PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM |
 				       PDO_FIXED_DUAL_ROLE |
 				       PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM |
 				       PDO_FIXED_DATA_SWAP)>;
-		op-sink-microwatt = <15000000>;
+		op-sink-microwatt = <5000000>;
 
 		ports {
 			#address-cells = <1>;
